<title>GERMANY: SGL says will raise dividend for 1996.</title>
<headline>SGL says will raise dividend for 1996.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>German carbon and graphite manufacturer SGL Carbon AG said on Monday it plans to pay a higher dividend for the business year 1996.</p>
<p>&quot;We will pay a higher dividend without a shadow of a doubt,&quot; management board chairman Robert Koehler told a news conference. But he declined to say how much higher the dividend would be.</p>
<p>For 1995, the company paid a dividend of 1.67 marks per share.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
